    "narrative": "The standout play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, whose elite score of 85.94 is driven by a massive matchup advantage against Zach Agnos. **Corbin Carroll** profiles as our primary engine for stolen bases and counting stats, benefiting from an expected #2 spot in the order and a favorable 5.15 xERA from the opposing arm. We are also leaning heavily on **James Wood** (63.41) and **Mickey Moniak** (60.60); **James Wood**\u2019s leadoff positioning and strong xwOBA provide a solid floor despite facing a left-handed arm, while **Mickey Moniak** overcomes a platoon disadvantage to maintain a strong score based on the weakness of Eduardo Rodriguez. **Gabriel Moreno** also provides sneaky upside (65.25) as a high-floor catcher play against the porous Agnos.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s slate was the utilization of **Kyle Karros** (55.22) in the utility spot. While **Kyle Karros** cleared the 50-point threshold, he sits precariously on the edge of our benching criteria due to a bottom-of-the-order assignment that suppresses his run-production potential. He was favored over other depth pieces due to the platoon edge, but remains the first candidate to be pulled if we feel the need to preserve game caps later in the week. We are keeping a close watch on **Austin Riley** (53.89); while his power potential is always present, his BvP struggles against Sandy Alcantara and a drop to the #7 spot in the lineup make him a marginal start that we are only playing because our bench options like **Josh Naylor** and **Brice Turang** are unavailable due to scheduling.\n\nRisk management is paramount today as we navigate a high volume of \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Austin Riley**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Mickey Moniak**, **James Wood**, and **Kyle Karros**. Any unexpected shift downward in the batting order for **Tyler Soderstrom** or **Austin Riley** could drop their efficiency scores below our 40-point floor. Furthermore, while we monitor our IR-stashed talent\u2014specifically **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story**\u2014we must remain disciplined with our remaining active roster spots, ensuring that **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** remain ready to rotate in as game caps allow.",
